<%# console.site-editor — wp-admin/site-editor.php. ⚠️ SERVER-SIDE SHELL ONLY this pass.
    The template/part browser, the block canvas and Global Styles editing are the deferred
    React island:  deferred: react-island (DEV-012, D-3).  The substrate it will edit
    already exists (Composition::Template, the theme.json four-origin cascade); this screen
    is the authenticated, authorized entry point and an honest inventory, not a fake editor. -%>
<div class="edit-bar">
  <span class="title">Editor</span>
</div>

<main class="canvas">
  <p class="placeholder-note">
    Site editor — <strong>deferred: react-island (DEV-012, D-3)</strong>. Template and Global
    Styles editing are not built this pass. The templates the active theme resolves are listed
    below (read-only) so the shell is truthful about what exists behind it.
  </p>

  <div class="doc">
    <% if @templates.present? %>
      <ul>
        <% @templates.each do |template| %>
          <li><code><%= template.slug %></code> — <%= template.theme_slug %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    <% else %>
      <%# P-LIST empty-state convention; the site editor's own list is not built. %>
      <p>No templates found.</p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</main>
